---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { ArrowRight02Icon } from '@hugeicons/core-free-icons';
import { getFonts } from '../lib/fonts';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import { MOODS, CLASSIFICATION_LABELS } from '../data/moods';
import { USE_CASE_LABELS, USE_CASES } from '../data/use-cases';

const fonts = await getFonts();
const count = fonts.length;

// One real entry to explain the three tag groups.
const example = fonts.find((f) => f.id === 'bricolage-grotesque') ?? fonts[0];
const ex = example.data;

const criteria = [
  {
    title: 'Used or seriously evaluated',
    body: "I've used it on a real project, or I've sat with it long enough to have a genuine opinion. That's the whole bar.",
  },
  {
    title: 'Open license',
    body: 'Free for commercial use under an open license, mostly the SIL Open Font License. No paid fonts, no affiliate links.',
  },
  {
    title: 'A useful note and a way to install it',
    body: 'The page says why the font is here, including what to watch out for, and gives copy-paste install snippets.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Why Fontlog exists, how fonts get in, and what the notes mean."
>
  <section class="grid items-center gap-10 pb-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16 lg:pb-16">
    <div>
      <h1
        class="text-[2.5rem] leading-[1.02] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-balance sm:text-6xl"
      >
        A small log. A more considered choice.
      </h1>
    </div>

    <figure
      data-specimen="sand"
      class="border-divider rounded-xl border p-6 sm:p-8"
      aria-label="Typographic sample: the three typefaces Fontlog is set in"
    >
      <p class="font-heading text-[5.5rem] leading-none font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-[7rem]" aria-hidden="true">
        Aa
      </p>
      <p class="font-heading mt-6 text-2xl leading-tight font-semibold">Bricolage Grotesque</p>
      <p class="font-body text-ink-2 mt-1 text-lg">Funnel Sans for the words in between.</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-ink-2 mt-1 text-base">Inconsolata for code, 0123456789</p>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <div class="prose-page space-y-6 text-lg leading-[1.7]">
    <p>
      For years, every project started with Bricolage Grotesque. I liked it, I knew it, and choosing
      something else could take an evening. I'd open a dozen specimen tabs, get stuck on licenses
      and install instructions, then go back to the font I already had.
    </p>

    <p>
      Fontlog keeps that search small. Every typeface here is one I've used or seriously evaluated,
      with a note on where it works and what to watch for. Try it on this site, find a pairing,
      and copy the setup into your project.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="mt-16 sm:mt-20" aria-labelledby="how-in">
    <h2 id="how-in" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">How a font gets in</h2>
    <ol class="mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3 md:gap-6">
      {
        criteria.map((c, i) => (
          <li class="border-ink border-t pt-4">
            <p class="font-mono text-ink-2 text-sm" aria-hidden="true">
              {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
            </p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl leading-tight font-semibold">{c.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-2 mt-2 max-w-[44ch]">{c.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-16 sm:mt-20" aria-labelledby="notes">
    <div class="prose-page space-y-6 text-lg leading-[1.7]">
      <h2 id="notes" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Reading an entry</h2>
      <p>
        Each entry explains why I'd use the font and where I'd be careful. You'll find:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>A live preview you can type your own text into.</li>
        <li>The license in one plain-English sentence, with a link to the real thing.</li>
        <li>
          Copy-paste install snippets: npm / Fontsource, <code class="font-mono text-[0.95em]">next/font</code>,
          Google Fonts, and a self-host template.
        </li>
        <li>Real sites using the font, when I've found good ones.</li>
        <li>
          Suggested uses, with a reason for each.
        </li>
        <li>A few &ldquo;if you like this, try&rdquo; pointers.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h3 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Style, Mood and Good for</h3>
    <p class="text-ink-2 mt-2 max-w-[66ch]">
      Three separate ways to filter the catalogue. Here they are on one real entry,
      <a href={`/fonts/${example.id}`} class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">{ex.name}</a>.
    </p>

    <dl class="panel mt-6 grid divide-y divide-divider md:grid-cols-3 md:divide-x md:divide-y-0">
      <div class="p-5">
        <dt class="text-ink-2 text-sm font-medium">Style</dt>
        <dd class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold">{CLASSIFICATION_LABELS[ex.classification]}</dd>
        <dd class="meta mt-2">
          The broad family: sans, serif, mono or display.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="p-5">
        <dt class="text-ink-2 text-sm font-medium">Mood</dt>
        <dd class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold capitalize">{ex.moods.join(', ')}</dd>
        <dd class="meta mt-2">
          How it feels: {MOODS.slice(0, -1).join(', ')}, or {MOODS.at(-1)}. Start here when you
          know the feeling you want but haven't found the font.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="p-5">
        <dt class="text-ink-2 text-sm font-medium">Good for</dt>
        <dd class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold">
          {ex.bestFor.map((b) => USE_CASE_LABELS[b.use]).join(', ')}
        </dd>
        <dd class="meta mt-2">
          The job it does, not how it feels: {USE_CASES.map((u) => USE_CASE_LABELS[u]).join(', ')}.
          Each one comes with a reason on the font's page.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <p class="text-ink-2 mt-6 max-w-[66ch]">
      These are judgement calls, not rules: plenty of good typefaces work far outside the boxes
      I've put them in. A claim I can't justify in a sentence doesn't get made.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-16 sm:mt-20" aria-labelledby="open">
    <div class="prose-page space-y-6 text-lg leading-[1.7]">
      <h2 id="open" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Everything is open</h2>
      <p>
        Every typeface listed is free for commercial use under an open license (mostly the SIL Open
        Font License). There are {count} in the catalogue. I add another when I find one I'd use.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary group">
        Browse the catalogue
        <Icon icon={ArrowRight02Icon} size={18} class="arrow" />
      </a>
      <a href={SITE.repo} class="btn btn-quiet" rel="noopener">View the source on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
